---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, REPO_URL, url } from '../data/site';
---
<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What VibeFlow, the Mac menu bar app, does with your data: it runs on your Mac, has no server and no account, and sends text only to the providers you choose."
  path="privacy/"
  updated="November 5, 2026"
>
  <p>
    VibeFlow is a macOS menu bar app published by {PUBLISHER} ("we"). It runs entirely on your
    Mac. We do not operate a server for it, there is no VibeFlow account, and we do not collect,
    sell or share your data. This policy explains what the app touches and where it goes.
  </p>

  <h2>What stays on your Mac</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Settings, reading and dictation history, focus logs and transcripts are stored locally in
      your user Library (UserDefaults and Application Support/VibeFlow).</li>
    <li>API keys you enter and your Google sign-in tokens are stored in the macOS Keychain.</li>
    <li>Deleting the app and these files removes everything. We have no copy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Text and audio you send to voice and AI providers</h2>
  <p>
    When you read text aloud, dictate, or use smart read, VibeFlow sends that text or audio
    directly from your Mac to the provider you configured, using your own API key: ElevenLabs
    (speech and transcription), Groq (dictation) or Anthropic (smart read and summaries). Apple's
    built-in voices work offline and send nothing. Each provider handles that data under its own
    privacy policy. We never see it.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Calendar (Meetings)</h2>
  <p>
    The optional Meetings feature shows your next meeting in the menu bar. If you choose
    "Sign in with Google", VibeFlow asks for one permission, <strong>read-only access to your
    calendars</strong> (<code>calendar.readonly</code>), and uses it only to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>list your calendars so you can pick which ones to watch, and</li>
    <li>read today's and upcoming events (title, time, organizer, attendees' response, and the
      Meet, Zoom or Teams link) to show the next meeting and a Join button.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Calendar data is requested directly from Google by the app on your Mac, held in memory while
    the app runs, and never written to disk, sent to us, sent to any AI provider, or shared with
    anyone. VibeFlow never creates, changes or deletes calendar events. Your sign-in tokens stay
    in your Keychain. Signing out in Settings &gt; Meetings deletes them from your Mac; to also
    remove VibeFlow's access on Google's side, visit
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    VibeFlow's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API
    Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. Google user data is
    not used for advertising, not used to train AI or machine learning models, and not read by
    any person.
  </p>

  <h2>Feedback and crash reports</h2>
  <p>
    If the app crashes, or you press Send Feedback, a report goes to Sentry (EU region), which we
    use to fix bugs. Reports contain the app version, macOS version, technical logs and anything
    you type into the feedback form. The app never logs the text you read or dictate, smart read
    answers, or meeting titles, so they are not in these reports.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and the website</h2>
  <p>
    The app checks GitHub for updates (Sparkle), which sends your app and macOS version. This
    website is hosted on GitHub Pages, sets no cookies and runs no analytics.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>VibeFlow is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We will post changes to this policy on this page and update the date above. Questions or
    requests: open an issue at <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>github.com/floo-one/vibeflow</a>
    or use Send Feedback in the app. See also the <a href={url('terms/')}>Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
